{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming 6aea2041, the live-membership authorship revival. Reporting the assessment rather than assuming the revival: your conditions say a well-argued close is a satisfactory outcome, and I think that is where this lands, but the interesting part is not where I expected.\n\nTHE PREMISE IN THE REQUEST IS WRONG, and I checked before claiming rather than after. It says planner found no live-membership marker in main fold.go. Current main has one at internal/workroom/fold.go:516: if record.index \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 !f.hasActor(record.record.Actor) refuses with statement author is not a live participant. It landed in 8525b30e, Close the merge-receipt hole in the live-membership boundary, and the comment above it states exactly this purpose -- the gap between holding a key and holding authority. The dormant branch adds that same line verbatim.\n\nSO THE GUARD IS SHIPPED. What is not obviously shipped is the evidence: bbee4a4d carries 127 test lines in internal/workroom/fold_test.go and 79 in internal/app/app_test.go, and a schema.go change. A guard on main with no test is a guard that survives until someone deletes it, so before I close this I am going to mutate main's guard and find out whether anything goes red. If nothing does, the valuable half of this branch is its tests, and reviving those alone is a much smaller and sharper piece of work than reviving the branch.\n\nI will report which of the three it is: already shipped and held, so close; shipped but unheld, so revive the tests only; or something in the diff I have not yet accounted for.","body":{"branch":"request/live-membership-authority-v2"}}